From f994b8207f33ac5756a8fc1037ae307a9ee844a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AsdreamChan <53651187+AsdreamChan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] configs: imx8mp_frdm: shorten the autoboot delay to one
 second

The autoboot countdown was the longest stage between the SPL banner and
"Starting kernel": 4.9 s of 9.1 s, timed from the serial console.

One second still lets autoboot be stopped by hand. A key held down while
the board resets is already waiting when the countdown starts, so it
stops autoboot whatever the delay.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]
Signed-off-by: AsdreamChan <53651187+AsdreamChan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 configs/imx8mp_frdm_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/imx8mp_frdm_defconfig b/configs/imx8mp_frdm_defconfig
index 87694560..7dd36957 100644
--- a/configs/imx8mp_frdm_defconfig
+++ b/configs/imx8mp_frdm_defconfig
@@ -214,3 +214,4 @@ CONFIG_EFI_HAVE_CAPSULE_UPDATE=y
 CONFIG_FIT_SIGNATURE=y
 
 CONFIG_BOOTDEV_ETH=n
+CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=1
-- 
2.43.0

